title: Pam_Boots
---
<<set_left CharacterManager Pamella>>
<<wait .15>>
<<set_right CharacterManager Francine>>
<<wait .15>>
<<left CharacterManager>>
<<wait .15>>
Pamella: I’m just not in the mood today, Francine. I’m in mourning.
<<right CharacterManager>>
<<wait .15>>
Francine: Are you okay?
<<left CharacterManager>>
<<wait .15>>
Pamella: No, obviously. 
She covers her mouth in a valiant effort to stifle her tears…Then she points down at her feet. 
Pamella: Just… look!
You do.
…you don’t understand what you’re supposed to be looking at. 
Pamella: Are you blind? The boots, Francine. The boots!
<<right CharacterManager>>
<<wait .15>>
Francine: They… look nice? Like normal?
<<left CharacterManager>>
<<wait .15>>
Pamella: They’re COMPLETELY DIFFERENT. Look – the heel on my normal boots broke last night, so I had to resort to my backups. It’s completely throwing off the outfit – my go-tos are latte brown, and these are all the way to toffee brown.
<<right CharacterManager>>
<<wait .15>>
Francine: I’m sorry for your loss?
Pam sighs, frowning down at her feet.
<<left CharacterManager>>
<<wait .15>>
Pamella: Thanks, France. I’m not sure how I’ll recover, though.
<<ending CharacterManager>>
===
